    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102236" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾰλᾰ-πείριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τλάω, πεῖρα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who has suffered much,
				much-suffering</i>, not in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεῖνος τ. ἐνθάδ᾽ ἱκάνω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.24
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				17.84
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκέτης τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				6.193
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				14.511
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωχὸς τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				10.66
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>vagrant, vagabond</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				10.10
			</span></i>.</div>
